{
  "description": "Rows for the hook client's pre-edit of a path with the workspace file .coherence/hook_on_held set to refuse (the two setting rows aside). Each row has: name, unique; stage, before_post for an exit of the decision before the opted-in POST /hooks/pre-edit is sent, or post for the answer to that POST; caller, the Claude Code payload's session_id and agent_id (null when absent); either http, the coordinator's {status, body} with body as parsed JSON, or outcome, a named outcome; and expected, the outcome class. Named outcomes before the POST, in the order the decision meets them: setting_off (absent, empty or displace); setting_unknown (any other value but refuse); not_strict (strict under no fold profile, or no strict entries); no_port (no .coherence directory, no server.pid, or a server.pid with no port line); died_at_resolve (any other failure to resolve the endpoint, such as a dead coordinator or a state file that cannot be read); timeout, refused and malformed_answer (GET /status?detail=metrics timed out, had its connection refused, or answered a body that is not a JSON object); status_non_2xx (that GET answered a non-2xx status); status_key_absent (that GET answered 2xx without pre_edit_if_unheld: true); not_strict_under_coordinator_profile (strict under some fold profile, not under the one the coordinator reports); malformed_agent_id (a present agent_id that is not a string of 1-64 chars of [A-Za-z0-9_-]). Named outcomes after the POST: timeout; refused; departed (the coordinator went away mid-request, so the connection was reset or closed with no answer); malformed_answer (a body that is not a JSON object). Outcome classes: today (the requests, stdout and stderr of a hook that never opted in); today_and_stderr_line (the same plus one stderr line); relay_admit and relay_deny (stdout is the coordinator's body as received); holder_deny, parent_deny and unavailable_deny (stdout is the deny of holder_deny.json, parent_deny.json or unavailable_deny.json, rendered for the edited path and, for holder_deny, the row's holder_agent_id).",
